From f0147e0000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0147e] evergo: repair a NULL thread_group at the assertion site

0145e (birth) and 0146e (coalition source) both failed to stop the v72 boot
(k85425c6f) from hitting

    thread_group.c:171 Assertion failed: thread->thread_group != NULL

and the SWEET COAL diagnostic added by 0146e never printed.  So the NULL is
not coming from task_coalition_get_thread_group() at all - some other path
writes it (bank voucher, auto-join, work-interval, or a thread that was never
passed through thread_group_init_thread()).  Guessing one more upstream site
has already burned two rounds.

Fix it where it actually hurts: sched_clutch_for_thread() is the assertion
site and lives in thread_group.c, so it can see tg_system.  If a thread shows
up with a NULL group, assign tg_system right there and log the thread and the
caller.  That both keeps the boot alive and finally tells us who is passing
the bad thread.

This is safe for sched_clutch.c:2420's
    assert(thread->thread_group == clutch->sc_tg)
because the returned clutch belongs to tg_system and sc_tg is tg_system, so
both sides now agree.  tg_system is created by thread_group_init() (early in
startup.c) and never released; guard against a NULL tg_system just in case a
call arrives before that.

0145e and 0146e stay as defence in depth.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/thread_group.c b/osfmk/kern/thread_group.c
index f04b813..c44ff26 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/thread_group.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/thread_group.c
@@ -168,6 +168,31 @@ thread_group_init(void)
 sched_clutch_t
 sched_clutch_for_thread(thread_t thread)
 {
+#if defined(SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * evergo (0147e): v70/v71/v72 all die on the assertion below while
+	 * neither the birth-time guard (0145e) nor the coalition-source
+	 * fallback (0146e) fires - so some other path hands us a thread whose
+	 * group is NULL.  Repair it here (this function can see tg_system) and
+	 * name the caller; the printed address tells us which sched_clutch
+	 * path is responsible so the real writer can be found next.
+	 */
+	if (__improbable(thread->thread_group == NULL)) {
+		static thread_t last_thread;
+		if (last_thread != thread) {
+			last_thread = thread;
+			printf("SWEET TG2: thread %p had NULL group, caller %p "
+			    "- using system\n", thread,
+			    __builtin_return_address(0));
+		}
+		if (__improbable(tg_system == NULL)) {
+			/* before thread_group_init(): nothing sane to hand back */
+			printf("SWEET TG2: tg_system not ready yet\n");
+		} else {
+			thread->thread_group = tg_system;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 	assert(thread->thread_group != NULL);
 	return &(thread->thread_group->tg_sched_clutch);
 }
